# NVRAM_PROGRAMMER: the in-circuit NVRAM programmer, a Teensy++ 2.0 (AT90USB1286), its pins
# numbered by their port names as printed on the Teensy. Transcribed from nvram-programmer
# CLAUDE.md's pin table and src/main.cpp (github.com/sparkybrit/nvram-programmer).
# Bus pins are tri_state: released whenever the programmer does not own the bus. /RESET is
# open drain (DDR toggled). Powered from the SBC 5 V (USB power trace cut).
# PD6 (A6) also carries the Teensy LED to ground: see sparky1 CLAUDE.md, To Do.
# Every pad of the two edge rows and the PA block is listed, the unused ones NC, so the symbol
# can draw them where they are (nvram-programmer images/teensy-pinout.svg, top view, USB end
# down). The two edge GND pads are GND1 (left edge, beside AREF) and GND2 (right edge, by PB7).
# The other interior pads (PE4, PE5, ALE and the rest) are not drawn there and not listed.
#
# pin  name  type
PD0 A0 tri_state
PD1 A1 tri_state
PD2 A2 tri_state
PD3 A3 tri_state
PD4 A4 tri_state
PD5 A5 tri_state
PD6 A6 tri_state
PD7 A7 tri_state
PC0 A8 tri_state
PC1 A9 tri_state
PC2 A10 tri_state
PC3 A11 tri_state
PC4 A12 tri_state
PC5 A13 tri_state
PC6 A14 tri_state
PC7 A15 tri_state
PB0 A16 tri_state
PB1 A17 tri_state
PB2 A18 tri_state
PB5 A24 tri_state
PB6 A25 tri_state
PF0 D0 bidirectional
PF1 D1 bidirectional
PF2 D2 bidirectional
PF3 D3 bidirectional
PF4 D4 bidirectional
PF5 D5 bidirectional
PF6 D6 bidirectional
PF7 D7 bidirectional
PA0 ~{AS} tri_state
PA2 ~{WE} tri_state
PA3 FC0 tri_state
PA4 FC1 tri_state
PA5 FC2 tri_state
PE0 ~{BR} output
PE1 ~{BGACK} output
PE6 ~{RESET} open_collector
PE7 ~{BG} input
VCC +5V power_in
GND1 GND power_in
GND2 GND power_in
AREF AREF passive
PB3 NC no_connect
PB4 NC no_connect
PB7 NC no_connect
PA1 NC no_connect
PA6 NC no_connect
PA7 NC no_connect
